### Food Delivery Platform - Promotion Service (coupons)
### Written for the VS Code "REST Client" extension (named requests pass ids between calls).
###
### Platform admins create and manage coupons; customers see the coupons on offer and apply one to their cart
### (order-service.http, step 8a). At checkout order-service reserves one use of the coupon; the order's events
### then decide whether the use counts: OrderCreated -> APPLIED, delivered -> REDEEMED, cancelled -> RELEASED.
### A reservation that never got an order is given back after 30 minutes (EXPIRED).
###
### Caller identity: the access token of an admin's sign-in below (Authorization: Bearer) for /admin/**.

@gateway = http://localhost:8080
# The services' shared secret of the internal APIs: the dev profile's value (INTERNAL_SERVICE_TOKEN elsewhere)
@internalServiceToken = dev-internal-service-token
@service = http://localhost:8089
@adminEmail = admin@fooddelivery.local
@adminPassword = ChangeMe123
# Every call carries the access token of a sign-in above (valid 15 minutes: sign in again after that).
@adminToken = {{adminLogin.response.body.$.accessToken}}
@couponId = {{createCoupon.response.body.$.id}}
@couponVersion = {{createCoupon.response.body.$.version}}


### ============================ ADMIN ============================

### 1. Admin login -> adminToken
# @name adminLogin
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{adminEmail}}", "password": "{{adminPassword}}" }

### 2. Create a coupon: 100 off orders of 499 or more, once per customer, 1000 uses (409 if the code exists)
###    Dates are calendar days in the business time zone (Asia/Kolkata); change them to include today.
# @name createCoupon
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/admin/coupons
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "code": "WELCOME100",
  "description": "100 off your first order",
  "discountType": "FIXED",
  "discountValue": 100,
  "minOrderAmount": 499,
  "validFrom": "2026-10-01",
  "validUntil": "2026-12-31",
  "usageLimit": 1000,
  "perCustomerLimit": 1
}

### 3. A percentage coupon for one restaurant: 20% off, at most 150 (set restaurantId to one of yours)
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/admin/coupons
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "code": "SPICE20",
  "description": "20% off at Spice Hub",
  "discountType": "PERCENTAGE",
  "discountValue": 20,
  "maxDiscount": 150,
  "minOrderAmount": 0,
  "restaurantId": 1,
  "validFrom": "2026-10-01",
  "validUntil": "2026-10-31",
  "usageLimit": 500,
  "perCustomerLimit": 3
}

### 4. Search coupons (code contains, status, discountType, restaurantId, validOn=a date); each shows its availability
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/admin/coupons?code=welcome&status=ACTIVE&page=0&size=20
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 5. Coupon details with usage: uses by status, discount given, distinct customers
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/admin/coupons/{{couponId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 6. Change the terms (send the version you read; 409 if someone changed it meanwhile).
###    The code cannot change; the usage limit cannot go below the uses already taken.
PUT {{gateway}}/api/v1/admin/coupons/{{couponId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "description": "100 off your first order",
  "discountType": "FIXED",
  "discountValue": 100,
  "minOrderAmount": 399,
  "validFrom": "2026-10-01",
  "validUntil": "2026-12-31",
  "usageLimit": 2000,
  "perCustomerLimit": 1,
  "version": {{couponVersion}}
}

### 7. Pause the coupon (customers get "This coupon is not active")
PUT {{gateway}}/api/v1/admin/coupons/{{couponId}}/deactivate
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reason": "Campaign paused" }

### 8. Resume it
PUT {{gateway}}/api/v1/admin/coupons/{{couponId}}/activate
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reason": "Campaign resumed" }

### 9. Who used it, and what happened to each use (status: RESERVED, APPLIED, REDEEMED, RELEASED, EXPIRED)
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/admin/coupons/{{couponId}}/redemptions?page=0&size=20
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 10. Audit trail of the coupon
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/admin/coupons/{{couponId}}/audit-logs
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}


### ============================ CUSTOMER ============================

### 11. Coupons on offer today (optionally only those valid at one restaurant)
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/coupons?restaurantId=1


### ===================== INTERNAL (order-service) =====================
### Not routed by the gateway: called directly on the service port.

### 12. Would the coupon work for this cart? (changes nothing)
POST {{service}}/api/v1/internal/coupons/check
X-Service-Token: {{internalServiceToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "code": "WELCOME100", "customerId": 999, "restaurantId": 1, "itemsTotal": 379.00 }

### 13. Reserve one use for a checkout (the same key again returns the same reservation)
POST {{service}}/api/v1/internal/coupon-reservations
X-Service-Token: {{internalServiceToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reservationKey": "checkout:999:http-file-test", "code": "WELCOME100", "customerId": 999, "restaurantId": 1, "itemsTotal": 599.00 }

### 14. The checkout failed: give the use back (EXPIRED)
DELETE {{service}}/api/v1/internal/coupon-reservations/checkout:999:http-file-test
X-Service-Token: {{internalServiceToken}}
